// COVERS DomainLexerGrammar: Enum, as
//
// `as` is reachable only as an IDENTIFIER -- DomainParserGrammar lists AS in its identifier
// rule, and the one construct that uses the AS token proper is the treePath alias, which
// belongs to the `projects` projection form that the walker NPEs on. So the surface a user
// can actually reach is `as` used as a property name.
//
// Same reason as keyword-as-identifier.pure: a parser that dispatches on the token before
// trying the identifier arm accepts everything here except a property called `as`.
###Pure
Enum fixture::domain::Region
{
   EMEA,
   APAC,
   AMERICAS
}

Enum fixture::domain::Side
{
   BUY,
   SELL
}

Class fixture::domain::Trade
{
   as: String[1];
   region: fixture::domain::Region[1];
   side: fixture::domain::Side[1];
}
